---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Windows from '../components/Windows.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="Who is behind Dack Builds and what this site is for.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="article-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1>One apartment, a lot of wiring.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Dack Builds is where I write up the smart home and homelab projects I run in a rented apartment, including the
        parts that did not work the first time.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I am Dack. I have spent more than ten years fixing and supporting consumer tech, and now I mostly build things
        that talk to Home Assistant. Because I rent, every project has a rule: nothing permanent, nothing that costs me
        the deposit, and nothing that leaves a hole in the wall.
      </p>
      <h2>What you will find here</h2>
      <p>
        Build logs with the real parts list, the dead ends, and the fix that finally worked. A post usually starts with
        a problem I actually had, like a ceiling fan with no smart option or an intercom that only knows how to buzz.
      </p>
      <h2>How I handle affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        Some links earn me a small commission. A post that has them says so at the top, and I do not pick a product
        because it pays. If something is bad, I say so.
      </p>
      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Write to <a href="mailto:hello@dackbuilds.com">hello@dackbuilds.com</a>. I read everything, and I answer when I
        have something useful to say.
      </p>
    </div>

    <Windows />
  </div>
</Base>
